From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77705_usbc_ilim: 9 V USB-PD and battery
 temperature bands

The MAX77705's USB-C firmware agrees a 5 V PD contract on its own (the
Galaxy Tab S7's Samsung charger offers 5/9/15/20 V fixed and three PPS
ranges). Stock then moves to the fixed 9 V PDO through the firmware's
command interface; its battery table gives 9 V a 1650 mA input limit
(15 W) and 3150 mA charge current. Do the same:
- on the firmware's 5 V PSRDY event, read the source's PDOs with
  OPCODE_CURRENT_SRCCAP (0x30), reply at 0x51;
- if there is a fixed 9 V PDO worth more than the 5 V TA's 9 W, set the
  9 V input limit first (it is safe at 5 V too), then request that PDO
  with OPCODE_SRCCAP_REQUEST (0x32);
- only once the firmware reports the new contract ready (PSRDY again)
  and its own VBUS ADC reads 8.5-9.5 V, raise the charge current to
  3150 mA;
- a refused request (0xfe/0xff), no 9 V within 3 s, or VBUS leaving 9 V
  returns to the 5 V limits. Each attach starts again at 5 V.

Only fixed PDOs up to 9 V are used (stock AVAILABLE_VOLTAGE); stock's PPS
path goes through a separate direct charger. The regmap now allows writes
to the three interrupt masks and the command buffer (0x21-0x41) only, and
the only commands sent are 0x30 and 0x32.

The mainline charger has no battery temperature handling, so apply the
stock bands (0.1 C) through the charge current:
- 15-42 C: normal, 9 V allowed;
- 42-50 C: 1000 mA, below stock's 2750 mA because the float voltage
  cannot be lowered as stock does;
- 5-15 C: 1850 mA; 0-5 C: 750 mA;
- above 50 C or below 0 C: 100 mA, the charger's minimum;
with stock's recovery thresholds, re-checked every 30 s while attached.
Outside the normal band no 9 V is requested.

The temperature comes from the battery thermistor on the PMIC ADC
("batt-therm" io-channel; on gts7l this is PM8150L AMUX_THM1_100K_PU,
stock sec-battery's "adc-temp"). The MAX77705 fuel gauge's own
temperature is not wired to it on this board and reads a constant 33.5 C.
Without a plausible reading (-40 to 100 C) the driver requests no 9 V and
charges at 1000 mA at most. Kconfig now depends on IIO.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -644,13 +644,15 @@
 
 config CHARGER_MAX77705_USBC_ILIM
 	tristate "Maxim MAX77705 USB-C input current selection"
-	depends on CHARGER_MAX77705 && I2C
+	depends on CHARGER_MAX77705 && I2C && IIO
 	select REGMAP_I2C
 	help
 	  Say Y to set the MAX77705 charger's input and charge current from
 	  what the chip's USB-C block detects (BC1.2 charger type and the
-	  Type-C current advertised on CC). Without it the charger stays at
-	  its power-on input limit. No USB-PD negotiation is done.
+	  Type-C current advertised on CC), and to move a USB-PD source to its
+	  fixed 9 V PDO through the block's firmware. Charging follows the
+	  battery temperature, read from the battery thermistor's ADC channel.
+	  Without it the charger stays at its power-on input limit.
 
 config CHARGER_MAX77759
 	tristate "Maxim MAX77759 battery charger driver"
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_usbc_ilim.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_usbc_ilim.c
